# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.net14, WIFID=1, connsys_step=17, XNU_SECS=118: the pictures of Settings.
# Run 80 (rc.jobs.net12, logs/lancelot-connsys30.log) got the first one at last -- 86 lines of fbjpg,
# logs/settings1.jpg -- but it was Wallet: the tap at 0.615 0.71 of the home screen lands on the icon
# the default layout puts there (Wallet is iconLists[0][16] in SpringBoard.app's
# DefaultIconState~iphone.plist, Settings is [17], and the two folders at [0] and [1] do not sit where
# the list says). So Settings is not found by tapping: it is launched, as battery_test's "launch" step
# does (SpringBoardServices' SBSLaunchApplicationWithIdentifier, the program signed with
# com.apple.springboard.opensensitiveurl), and its Wi-Fi page is opened with "open prefs:root=WIFI"
# (SBSOpenSensitiveURLAndUnlock). No icon and no row is guessed.
#
# The network is brought up first so the pane has something to show; fbwait waits for the first swap
# (~81 s) and 16 s more for the first real frame (run 76: swap 1 has no surfaces, swap 2 came 13.7 s
# later). fbgrab is still the last thing: the JPEG goes to the console in base64 and the log keeps the
# last ~261 KB. XNU_SECS=118 ends the run about 5 s after the second picture.
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 22
/redwood/bin/net_test dhcp en0 waitaddr en0 10
/redwood/bin/net_test fetch http://example.com/ 20
/redwood/bin/net_test fbwait 60
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 16
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 200
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 3
/redwood/bin/battery_test launch com.apple.Preferences
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 12
/redwood/bin/fbgrab -log settings 300 0.4
/redwood/bin/battery_test open prefs:root=WIFI
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 8
/redwood/bin/fbgrab -log wifi 300 0.4